Package: phpr-cli
Architecture: any
Depends: libgd3, libtidy58, ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Provides: php-cli, php8.5-cli, php-json, php8.5-json
Conflicts: php8.5-cli
Replaces: php8.5-cli
Description: command-line interpreter for PHP scripts (Rust reimplementation)
 phpr is a from-scratch reimplementation of PHP 8.5.7 in Rust (the
 php-rust project). It runs unmodified PHP scripts with the same
 observable behaviour as the reference interpreter, byte-for-byte for
 everything that lands in PHP strings and output streams.
 .
 This package installs the /usr/bin/phpr interpreter and registers it
 with update-alternatives as /usr/bin/php (priority 85, the 8.5 slot),
 so tooling that invokes "php" keeps working. It can coexist with the
 packaged php8.4-cli / php8.6-cli; it conflicts with php8.5-cli, whose
 package name it also Provides.
 .
 Known gaps vs the reference CLI (deliberate, documented in
 /usr/share/doc/phpr-cli/README.Debian): no php.ini is read, the
 -v/-m/-i/-l/-w/--ini switches are not implemented, and php8.5-*
 extension modules from the archive have no effect on phpr.

Package: phpr-server
Architecture: any
Depends: libgd3, libtidy58, ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: standalone PHP web server (php -S work-alike)
 php-server is the web SAPI of the php-rust project: a standalone HTTP
 server (a work-alike of "php -S") that serves a document root and
 executes PHP requests via the phpr engine, in two modes: the
 sequential cli-server mode and an Axum-based multi-worker mode
 (shared FIFO queue, one fresh VM per request).
 .
 This is NOT FastCGI: it does not speak the FPM protocol and therefore
 does not replace php8.5-fpm behind nginx/Apache fastcgi_pass. Front
 it with any reverse proxy over plain HTTP instead. The service runs
 as www-data and is configured through /etc/default/phpr-server
 (host, port, document root, worker count).
